dia/thumbs/amr-ibn-al-as.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amr ibn al-As</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amr ibn al-As was an Arab commander and companion of the Prophet Muhammad.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amritsar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amritsar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amritsar</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Amritsar is a city in the Punjab region of north-western India and the spiritual centre of Sikhism, home to the Harmandir Sahib, or Golden Temple.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/amshuvarman"><span class="enc-name">Amshuvarman</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amshuvarman was a ruler of Nepal in the Licchavi period, first a powerful minister under King Shivadeva I and then holder of royal titles.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/amsivarii"><span class="enc-name">Amsivarii</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Amsivarii were a Germanic people living near the river Ems in north-western Germany in the 1st century CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amsterdam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amsterdam</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Amsterdam is the capital of the Netherlands and was the commercial and financial heart of the Dutch Republic in the seventeenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amuktamalyada"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amuktamalyada.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amuktamalyada</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</sp